 "53": {
  "name": "Fort Abraham Lincoln State Park",
  "description": "Fort Abraham Lincoln State Park was the first state park established in North Dakota and is home to rich historical experiences. Visitors can gain insight into the lives of the Mandan Native Americans or experience what life was like as a frontier soldier. Hikers, bikers and horseback riders can enjoy extraordinary views from the high bluffs overlooking the confluence of the Heart River and Missouri River. Stay overnight along the shoreline in a cabin or one of over 100 campsites.",
