 "62": {
  "name": "Pembina Gorge State Park",
  "description": "A top destination for adventure seekers, the Pembina Gorge State Recreation Area encompasses 2,800 acres of public land in the scenic Pembina River Gorge. With steep valley cliffs towering over \nsmall, isolated prairies and pocketed wetlands surrounded by the largest continuous, undisturbed forest in North Dakota, the area\u2019s unique beauty offers many reasons to visit. Popular activities include mountain biking, hiking, riding OHV,\nhorseback riding and kayaking. Please be aware that the Pembina Gorge State Park campground is currently under construction and not yet available for camping reserva",
